      "title": "PolinRider Moves to Python with an Ethereum Calldata Loader",
      "summary": "PolinRider now plants a Python loader in GitHub repositories, hidden in a utils package or in conftest.py. When the file is imported, it reads the newest self-sent transaction of an Ethereum wallet, decodes the JavaScript stored in its input data, and runs it with Node.js. That JavaScript reads a second wallet to find the command and control server, then starts the next stage in a detached node -i process. SafeDep found the loader in 375 public repositories under 260 accounts, mostly small personal projects, and no package on PyPI or npm carries it. Because the loader uses only the standard library, dependency scans will not reveal it. Defenders should search repositories for the wallet and loader calls, treat any machine that ran the loader with Node.js as compromised, and clean the machines that push to affected repositories.",
